# GPU Training Setup Guide for Windows

## Step 1: Install Python 3.11 (Required for CUDA Support)

### Download Python 3.11
1. Go to: https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3119/
2. Download: Windows installer (64-bit)
3. **IMPORTANT**: Check "Add Python to PATH" during installation
4. Install with "Customize installation" → select "Install for all users"

### Verify Installation
```powershell
python3.11 --version
# Should show: Python 3.11.x
```

## Step 2: Create New Virtual Environment with Python 3.11

```powershell
# Navigate to ai-training directory
cd ai-training

# Create venv with Python 3.11
python3.11 -m venv venv311

# Activate venv
.\venv311\Scripts\activate

# Verify Python version
python --version
# Should show: Python 3.11.x
```

## Step 3: Install PyTorch with CUDA 12.1

```powershell
# Install PyTorch with CUDA support
pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121

# Verify CUDA is available
python -c "import torch; print(f'CUDA: {torch.cuda.is_available()}')"
# Should show: CUDA: True
```

## Step 4: Install Remaining Dependencies

```powershell
# Install from compatibility requirements
pip install -r requirements-compat.txt

# Install any missing packages
pip install psutil huggingface_hub defusedxml absl-py typer tokenizers==0.22.2
```

## Step 5: Verify GPU Setup

```powershell
# Run GPU check
python check_gpu.py

# Expected output:
# PyTorch: 2.x.x+cu121
# CUDA available: True
# CUDA version: 12.1
# GPU count: 1
# GPU name: [Your GPU name]
```

## Step 6: Train Models with GPU

```powershell
# Activate environment
.\venv311\Scripts\activate

# Train NLP model (will now use GPU)
python training/nlp/train_nlp.py

# Train other models
python training/self_fix/train_self_fix.py
python training/rag/train_rag.py
python training/ocr/train_ocr.py
python training/time_series/train_time_series.py
```

## Troubleshooting

### If Python 3.11 is not found:
```powershell
# Try these commands
py -3.11 --version
py -3.11 -m venv venv311
```

### If CUDA is still not available:
1. Update NVIDIA drivers: https://www.nvidia.com/Download/index.aspx
2. Verify GPU: `nvidia-smi`
3. Reinstall PyTorch with CUDA

### If pip install is slow:
```powershell
# Use faster mirror
pip install -r requirements-compat.txt -i https://pypi.tuna.tsinghua.edu.cn/simple
```

## Quick Setup Script

Once Python 3.11 is installed, run this automated setup:

```powershell
# Save as setup_gpu.ps1
python3.11 -m venv venv311
.\venv311\Scripts\activate
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install torch torchvision torchaudio --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu121
pip install -r requirements-compat.txt
pip install psutil huggingface_hub defusedxml absl-py typer tokenizers==0.22.2
python check_gpu.py
```

Execute with:
```powershell
.\setup_gpu.ps1
```

## Expected Results

With GPU training:
- **NLP model**: ~2-3 minutes (vs 15-20 min on CPU)
- **Self-Fix model**: ~10 seconds
- **RAG model**: ~1-2 minutes
- **OCR model**: ~3-5 minutes
- **Time Series**: ~30 seconds

**Total training time: ~10-15 minutes with GPU vs ~30-40 minutes on CPU**